	affiliations = {Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Jawaharlal Nehru Technological University, Telangana, Hyderabad, 500085, India},
	abstract = {With the fast development and utilization of cloud computing services, information security threats are emerging one after another. Traditional security approaches are not only context-oblivious but also not flexible to real-time cyber threats. Proposed Paper on Cloud Based Location Aware Security Framework with Machine Learning provides an overview of the model which leverages the power of Machine Learning along with proactive threat detection in Cloud security by integrating geospatial intelligence with machine learning-driven security analytics. In this paper, we present a model based on machine learning models and analyze user behavior, network anomalies and geospatial threat with real-time location data. It uses both supervised and unsupervised learning techniques to identify deviations from the standard behavior, forecast potential incursions, and enforce adaptive safety policies. Geofencing mechanisms add additional security to ensure that only those with explicit permission can access certain areas by providing specifically contextual location-based rules. This cloud-based architecture provides scalability, real-time processing, and effortless compatibility with existing security infrastructure. We detail the framework and validate it through a prototype field implementation and experimental evaluation demonstrating the framework's efficacy in the detection of advanced cyber-aggression threats. The analysis of performance indicates a greater degree of threat detection accuracy, fewer false positive occurrences, and quicker response times than with traditional security models. The use of machine learning greatly improves the capacity of the system to foresee and prevent security breaches before they happen. This study advances cloud defense mechanisms through a new machine learning-based, location-sensitive security system that can dynamically respond to new vulnerabilities. The study also highlights the capacity of AI-powered threat intelligence to improve cloud security. In future work, a deep-learning-based predictive model will be developed along with a combined deep learning and blockchain-based predictive model for advanced anomaly detection and data security and trust management respectively. © This article is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License. License details: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/},
	author_keywords = {Anomaly detection; Cloud security; Cybersecurity; Geospatial intelligence; Location aware security; Machine learning; Threat detection},
