	abstract = {Research on 6G communications has been initiated worldwide to build future mobile networks. Numerous issues confront 6G networks, including mobile devices with limited resources, challenging wireless resource management, very complex heterogeneous network designs, rapidly increasing computer and storage needs, and risks to privacy and security. Deploying artificial intelligence (AI) and blockchain in sixth generation (6G) may yield discoveries in improving network performance regarding privacy, efficiency, affordability, security, and other factors to address these issues. Green networks, which offer energy efficiency and excellent quality of service, are anticipated to develop from 6G. This study investigates the integration of blockchain and AI in the green 6G. The difficulties in integrating these technologies and possible solutions are also covered in the study. As a result of cyberattacks, these technologies’ applications will soon have such a profound effect on our society that it will be hard to imagine existence without them. When these two are combined, technology will change and various fields will be advanced that will help industry experts and academics, improving corporate structures and encouraging better service delivery. The study's conclusion offers insights into how this integration will develop going forward and how it can transform several sectors, including banking, healthcare, cybersecurity, cryptocurrency, and transportation. © 2026 by Begell House},
	author_keywords = {AI; blockchain; communication network; energy efficiency; green 6G},
	keywords = {Computer privacy; Cybersecurity; Green computing; Heterogeneous networks; Mobile telecommunication systems; Network security; Quality of service; Reviews; Service industry; Wireless networks; Block-chain; Communications networks; Energy; Green 6g; Green networks; Network design; Performance; Privacy and security; Quality-of-service; Wireless resource managements; Energy efficiency},
