	abstract = {Indoor air quality (IAQ) is a critical factor directly impacting the health, cognitive performance and readiness of military personnel, especially in enclosed operational environments, such as control centres, ships and armoured vehicles. Prolonged exposure to air pollutants such as carbon dioxide (CO2), volatile organic compounds (VOCs) and fine particulates can compromise decision-making capabilities and physical endurance, thus becoming a strategic risk to mission effectiveness. In the Malaysian context, tropical climate challenges such as consistently high humidity exacerbate IAQ risks, while conventional reactive management approaches are no longer adequate for the dynamic modern military environment. This conceptual paper proposes the integration of artificial intelligence (AI) as a paradigm shift for proactive IAQ management in military facilities. An integrated conceptual framework connecting IAQ, AI and military readiness is proposed, aiming to form a “military smart facility” ecosystem. This framework operates through three main mechanisms: (1) real-time IAQ monitoring using a network of smart sensors; (2) predictive analytics to anticipate pollution trends before they affect personnel; and (3) automated optimisation of ventilation and air filtration systems. This approach establishes a continuous optimisation loop, where AI analyses environmental and personnel performance data to maintain optimal readiness levels. However, its implementation faces several significant challenges, including technical issues involving existing infrastructure, cybersecurity, organisational culture barriers, as well as policy and ethical constraints on data usage. Overall, the integration of AI in IAQ management not only has the potential to enhance personnel well-being and performance but also strengthens national defence strategy through the concept of “preventive readiness”, and the development of more adaptive and resilient smart bases. © 2026 Science and Technology Research Institute for Defence (STRIDE). All rights reserved.},
