	abstract = {In the digital age, cybersecurity is essential to protect against cyber threats. Traditional tools, while crucial, often struggle to keep up with the rapidly evolving tactics of cybercriminals. Artificial Intelligence (AI) offers a transformative approach, enhancing real-time threat detection and response through advanced data analysis and machine learning. AI’s continuous ability to learn and adapt makes it vital for modern cybersecurity. However, its deployment raises ethical and legal challenges, including fairness, accountability, transparency, privacy, and data security issues. This literature survey provides a comprehensive overview of AI in cybersecurity, analyzes ethical and legal implications, and proposes guidelines to ensure responsible AI use, aiming to align with societal values and enhance trust in AI-driven cybersecurity solutions. © Copyright 2026 Taylor & Francis–All rights reserved.},
