	affiliations = {Robotics and Internet of Things Laboratory, Prince Sultan University, Riyadh, 12435, Saudi Arabia; RIADI Laboratory, National School of Computer Science, University of Manouba, Manouba, 2010, Tunisia},
	abstract = {The Internet of Medical Things (IoMT) has transformed modern healthcare through real-time monitoring, remote diagnostics, and efficient data sharing. However, its inherent exposure to diverse cyber-attacks poses critical security risks. Existing Artificial Intelligence (AI)-based defenses often fail to balance the dual requirements of computational efficiency for edge deployment and expressive modeling of long-range dependencies needed to capture complex cross-device intrusions. To address this challenge, we propose IDS-GraphMamba, a novel intrusion detection framework that uniquely integrates Mamba-style selective state-space modeling with Markov-based aggregation. The framework progresses in three stages: (i) graph construction from raw IoMT traffic, where communication flows are encoded as a row-stochastic transition matrix for stable sequential modeling; (ii) representation learning via Graph Mamba blocks, which combine directional convolutions, Markov-based message passing, and a Selective State-Space Module (SSSM) with adaptive gating to refine node embeddings while preventing oversmoothing; and (iii) flow classification using pooled graph embeddings and a lightweight softmax layer for real-time decision-making.The key contribution of IDS-GraphMamba is its ability to simultaneously model short-range dependencies, global structural interactions, and long-range temporal dynamics within IoMT traffic graphs. Extensive experiments confirm its superiority: IDS-GraphMamba attains 99.70 % accuracy, 99.30 % precision, and 99.13 % recall on the WUSTL-EHMS-2020 dataset, and 97.51 % accuracy, 97.06 % precision, and 97.76 % recall on the NF-BoT-IoT-v2 dataset. These results demonstrate that IDS-GraphMamba is not only highly accurate but also lightweight, scalable, and deployable in real-time on edge hardware, making it a practical and effective solution for strengthening IoMT cybersecurity. © 2025 Elsevier B.V.},
