	abstract = {The purpose of this research is to build the foundation for a conceptual Model that joins together Cybersecurity Awareness and Digital Safety for K-12 Schools and to determine if there are any ways in which Generative Artificial Intelligence (GenAI) can both create new types of risks and opportunities in the creation of a Digital Learning Environment that is Safe and Secure. The researchers will use a clearly defined method of concept analysis to systematically compile and critically evaluate the relevant literature in the fields of Cybersecurity Education, Digital Pedagogy, the Ethics of Artificial Intelligence and the Technology-related Policies of Saudi Arabia. The outcome from this analysis will be a clearly defined conceptual Model that delineates Cybersecurity Awareness into two distinct categories: 1) Passive Awareness and 2) Proactive Safety Cultures. Additionally, this research will identify the unique Cyber Threat Landscape that exists in K-12 Education in Saudi Arabia, develop a Theoretical Framework for the Integration of GenAI in K-12 Education in Saudi Arabia, and develop a Strategic Implementation Plan for the Use of Generative AI in Saudi Arabia to Enhance Teacher Training, Create Adaptive Learning Content for Digital Safety and Improve Institutional Monitoring. The researchers will also systematically address many of the Ethical and Practical Issues and Risks Associated with the Use of GenAI, including Data Privacy, Algorithmic Bias, and Overdependence. © Copyright 2026 Taylor & Francis–All rights reserved.},
