	abstract = {Hardware cyber security is a major issue in very large integrated circuits (ICs). The reliability and security of the system are vulnerable to counterfeit, forged, or defective ICs. The increasing complexity of digital and mixed-signal systems makes it difficult to develop effective techniques for evaluating and validating the reliability of ICs. In this manuscript, ensuring hardware reliability and security using terahertz very-large-scale-integration (VLSI)–based tree hierarchical deep convolutional neural network testing technology (EHRS-TZ-VLSI-THCNN) is proposed. A focused terahertz laser is used to scan a radio frequency integrated circuit (RFIC), and the response on a single pin is evaluated to generate two dimensional (2D) pictures. The secure picture data set is created by a data augmentation technique to train the proposed algorithm. The proposed EHRS-TZ-VLSI-THCNN approach achieves 25.26%, 31.74%, and 25.21% greater precision and 21.52%, 24.244%, and 25.65% better accuracy when compared to the existing models: AI-powered terahertz VLSI testing technology to ensure hardware safety (CNN-PT-VLSI-EHS), AI powered terahertz (THz) VLSI testing technology (PNDT-PT-VLSI-EHS), and AI powered THz testing technology for ensuring hardware cybersecurity (AI-PT-VLSI-EHS). © 2026 John Wiley & Sons Ltd.},
