	abstract = {The rapid proliferation of sophisticated and evolving cyber threats in today’s interconnected digital landscape has created an urgent need for advanced defense mechanisms capable of operating reliably under adversarial conditions and within highly dynamic environments. Traditional rule-based cybersecurity approaches are increasingly proving inadequate, as attackers now exploit machine learning vulnerabilities and use artificial intelligence (AI) to craft adaptive and intelligent threats. The aim of this study is to introduce a comprehensive AI-powered cybersecurity framework designed to enhance the resilience, adaptability, and interpretability of digital defense systems. The framework seamlessly integrates adversarial robustness, federated learning, differential privacy, and real-time interpretability to form robust multilayered defense architecture. By employing multi-task learning in combination with attention-based explainability, the proposed system enhances both the accuracy and transparency of threat detection processes. Specifically, three core methodologies are developed and evaluated: (I) Adversarial Robust Multi-Task Learning, which resists evasion attacks while improving decision clarity; (II) Federated Learning with Differential Privacy and Certified Robustness, which ensures collaborative model training without compromising data privacy; and (III) the hybrid Federated Adversarial Learning with Certified Attention (FALCA) framework, which unifies the strengths of the first two techniques for scalable, privacy-preserving, and interpretable security. Experimental results across centralized and distributed settings confirm substantial improvements in detection accuracy, adversarial resilience, and real-time response efficiency. This work underscores the transformative potential of AI in fortifying modern cybersecurity systems and offers a promising direction for future research and implementation. © 2026 The Author(s).},
	author_keywords = {Adversarial Robustness; Artificial Intelligence (AI); Certified Robustness; Cybersecurity; Differential Privacy; Explainable AI (XAI); FALCA Framework; Federated Learning; Intrusion Detection Systems (IDS); Machine Learning (ML); Real-time Inference; Threat Detection},
