	abstract = {This study reviews EDPACS, the EDP Audit, Control, and Security Newsletter, which is the oldest IT audit newsletter in the world. The goal is to evaluate its scholarly contributions over the last decade, from 2014 to 2024. We used the Scopus database as our main source and applied Biblioshiny for visualization, analyzing 274 publications. We examined factors such as publication trends, contributions from institutions, citation impact, and thematic evolution. The findings show a steady increase in annual output, with an average growth rate of 5.32 percent and a citation rate of 2.75 per document. The main contributions came from institutions in the United States, Morocco, and Germany. Highly cited works focused on themes like digital transformation, COBIT 2019, blockchain auditing, cybersecurity, and internal audit effectiveness. This indicates the journal’s growing importance in IT governance and risk management. Thematic mapping identified digital transformation, artificial intelligence, and ICT as key themes. Security, risk assessment, and digitization emerged as foundational themes. The results highlight EDPACS’s role as a link between academia and practice in audit, control, and security. This study provides a clear bibliometric view of the journal’s growth and suggests areas for future research. These areas include exploring new technologies, encouraging collaboration between industry and academia, and investigating policy frameworks in IT governance. © Copyright 2025 Taylor & Francis–All rights reserved.},
