	abstract = {The use of generative AI (GenAI) has become one of the most facilitating technologies of advanced data creation, intelligent decision-making, and automated processing of the content in the current edge-cloud computing environments. This survey explains recent studies that indicate the future promise of GenAI algorithms combined with edge-cloud middleware architectures, specifically in application areas, including cybersecurity, environmental monitoring, innovative media, and intelligent industry systems. These works use a number of generative models, such as large language models, diffusion models, and agent-based generative models, to assist in synthetic data generation, behavior simulation, data fusion, and intelligent content generation. The survey classifies the existing works based on the generative algorithms on which they are based, and evaluates their contribution to better middleware-assisted interoperability, scalability, and deterministic service support in heterogeneous systems. The findings show that GenAI-based middleware leads to a major enhancement of flexibility, scalability, and contextual understanding in complex and distributed environments. Nevertheless, the analyzed literature demonstrates the difficulties associated with the domain dependency, the reliability of the data, the verification of the produced results, and the explainability, which are significant to take into consideration when standardizing GenAI-assisted edge-cloud middleware in Industry 4.0 and deterministic communications. © 2017 IEEE.},
