	abstract = {The recent introduction of generative AI technologies has resulted in widespread adoption by individual users and organizations. These technologies possess the potential to transform many industries and organizational functions. However, few organizations are successfully implementing at scale and realizing benefits. Furthermore, there is growing concern regarding safety. This exploratory study of 16 interview with senior executives and employees delves into organizations’ implementation experience. Our findings demonstrate that several underlying factors, including the organization’s preparedness and specific implementation strategy, can critically impact the success of implementation. Furthermore, organizations experience various safety risks related to cybersecurity, privacy, ethics including misinformation, trust and transparency. This study highlights the importance of balancing the benefits of generative AI with comprehensive approaches to information risk management. We offer initial practical recommendations to maximize benefits while minimizing risks. We also highlight paths for future research to determine how to design interfaces to promote safe generative AI implementation. © 2026 Informa UK Limited, trading as Taylor & Francis Group.},
