	abstract = {Malware is one of the frequently occurring cyberattacks, with its increasing prevalence posing severe security threats. Malware traffic is generally asymmetrical compared to benign, which is always symmetrical. While many Artificial Intelligence techniques have been developed to detect malware, challenges in handling large, high-dimensional data remain unresolved. A high-performance malware detection system using the novel Weighted Ensemble Extreme Transformer Adaboost model integrated with advanced feature selection methodology is proposed in this paper. The Mirror Strategy boosted Golden Jackal Optimization effectively minimizes data dimensionality while preserving essential information. The proposed ensemble framework, combining XGBoost, Transformer models, and Adaboost, enhances predictive accuracy and robustness. Experimental results show the proposed model achieves an accuracy of 99.24%, outperforming DL-AMDet of 89.85%, EvadeDroid of 75.24%, KFFPDet of 92.36%, AMD-XAI-ML of 80.71%, DroidXGB of 78.52%, and Tuned XGBoost of 85.29%. Additionally, the proposed model achieves 99.14% precision, 99.03% recall, and a 99.08% F1-score, with reduced false positives and negatives. Also, the proposed model attains faster execution time, further supporting its applicability for real-time malware detection, contributing to enhanced cybersecurity in complex environments. © 2025 IETE.},
