	abstract = {Adversarial attack is a key concern for state-of-the-art artificial intelligence (AI), especially those used in image classification and computer vision. These attacks exploit minute changes in input, deceiving models into predicting incorrect outcomes and thereby compromising the accuracy, reliability, and security of AI-driven decision-making. This opening leads to concerns with respect to facial recognition, autonomous driving, and even digital forensics, as these are all high-stakes areas of interest. Although the research is starting to increase, an unfilled gap is being faced in strong and adaptive defense mechanisms that could support real-time resistance against both poisons and evasion-based attackers. In order to overcome this vulnerability factor, we offer the new ResilienceNet Adversarial Framework (RNAF) defense architecture that incorporates Deep Reinforcement Learning (DRL) in order to generate a dynamic and intelligent countermeasure to an adversarial attack. In its process, RNAF memorizes Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) to constantly subject the model to adversarial environments, so it can adjust its protection mechanisms during training. Another exclusive feature of RNAF is its module of adaptive steganalysis that improves the detection process by discovering concealed malignant elements on a pixel-by-pixel basis. Adversarial Robustness Toolbox (ART) is employed in creating and identifying adversarial perturbations to aid in the various evaluations of its robust systems. RNAF is compared in terms of CIFAR-10 on RNAF with other existing models of ResNet50, VGG16, and Timm on adversarial attacks such as Projected Gradient Descent (PGD) and Fast Gradient Sign Method (FGSM). Based on an experimental study, RNAF yields a clean accuracy of 95.7 and adversarial accuracy of 88.0, which demonstrates RNAF can outperform baseline models in such robustness, precision-recall, F1 score, and ROC-AUC measures. This innovation is based on the unique combination of adaptive steganalysis, a dynamic PPO-based patch defense and ART-based adversarial learning, a combination which has not been studied in prior literature. RNAF is an adaptive defense approach against evolving threats, its setting a new standard in robust AI for image systems unlike traditional approaches before. © 2013 IEEE.},
