	abstract = {The proliferation of renewable energy systems integrated with Industry 4.0 technologies has created unprecedented cybersecurity challenges in modern power grids. Traditional defense mechanisms fail to address the dynamic, distributed, and interconnected nature of contemporary renewable energy infrastructures. This paper presents an intelligent adaptive cyber defense framework that leverages a hybrid artificial intelligence approach combining supervised learning for known threat classification, unsupervised learning for anomaly detection, and reinforcement learning for autonomous threat mitigation. The proposed framework employs a dynamic graph-based representation of renewable energy grids, enabling real-time topology adaptation and comprehensive security monitoring. Mathematical optimization formulations balance cybersecurity effectiveness with operational efficiency while maintaining grid stability constraints. Extensive experimental validation using a comprehensive dataset of 40,000 cyber-attack instances demonstrates superior performance above 94.5% detection accuracy, 2.4% false positive rate, and 0.85-second response time. The framework achieves 91.6% grid stability maintenance and 87.4% mitigation efficiency, representing significant improvements of 29.2% and 29.1% respectively over conventional systems. Comparative analysis against ten state-of-the-art methods confirms the framework’s superiority across all performance metrics, establishing its viability for securing critical renewable energy infrastructure in Industry 4.0 environments. © 2013 IEEE.},
