	abstract = {Since the mid-twentieth century, Artificial Intelligence (AI) has made it possible for computer systems to learn from experience and perform tasks in a similar way to humans. Today, it is naturally being incorporated into people’s lives and into the operations of companies. The objective of this article is to show an overview of AI in the world, analyzing its growth, its impact on GDP and employment, as well as presenting its use in Ecuador. The study is of a documentary type, with a descriptive scope, and with a mixed approach. The main conclusion is that revenues are estimated for 2030 for hardware, software and AI services of more than 500 billion dollars. The biggest impact is on the GDP of China and the US with 26% and 14% respectively. The sectors with the greatest impact on GDP due to the use of AI are consumer goods, food and accommodation services with 9% and other services such as health, education, commercial, etc. with 12%. As for employment, it is more likely in jobs with greater physical effort or repetitive work than in jobs with intellectual effort, creativity or decision making. In Ecuador, there are advances in the use of AI in the sectors of Healthcare, Transport, Finance, Commerce and others such as security or cybersecurity. © 2023, Associacao Iberica de Sistemas e Tecnologias de Informacao. All rights reserved.},
